# Citation metadata. GitHub renders this as the repository's "Cite this
# repository" button. There is no paper behind tddlog yet, so this
# describes the software itself; `preferred-citation` redirects citations
# to one once it is written.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "tddlog: Exact Probabilistic Inference by Compilation into Tree Decision Diagrams"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Van den Broeck"
    given-names: "Guy"
    affiliation: "Computer Science Department, University of California, Los Angeles"
abstract: >-
  Exact probabilities for probabilistic Datalog programs: probabilistic
  facts, annotated disjunctions, and recursive rules with negation,
  comparisons and arithmetic. Front ends reduce ProbLog programs with
  function symbols and lists, Bayesian and Markov networks, Dice
  programs, Circulette netlists and LPADs to them.
  A program is ground, simplified, compiled bottom up into tree decision
  diagrams with the tididi library, and its queries are counted on the
  diagrams. A Rust library and command-line tool, with Python, C and
  WebAssembly bindings.
keywords:
  - probabilistic logic programming
  - ProbLog
  - probabilistic programming
  - Bayesian networks
  - knowledge compilation
  - decision diagrams
  - weighted model counting
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Tractables/tddlog"
url: "https://tractables.github.io/tddlog/"
version: 0.1.0
